This thesis provides: (1) a rigorous epistemic framework distinguishing THEOREM, CONJECTURE, NUMERICAL EVIDENCE, and HEURISTIC; (2) a reformulation of the QFIM–area problem as an integrability problem S \in \operatorname{Im}(\mathfrak{R} \circ \Phi_{L*}); (3) a precise statement of the QFIM–Area Integrability Conjecture; (4) a numerical benchmark with three models and five residuals; (5) a literature survey identifying what is established and what remains open; (6) explicit positioning relative to Yaman (2026) and Lee (2026).

